+/* PC3: EP0 RX-timeout grace window (usb/hcd_rp2040.patch).  A spurious
+ * RX_TIMEOUT can be the SIE's single shared handshake latch - ACK_REC /
+ * RX_TIMEOUT / DATA_SEQ_ERROR, one register for EPX and the interrupt-endpoint
+ * poller - overwritten by an interrupt-endpoint poll before this handler reads
+ * it (TinyUSB #3533): the control transfer was ACK'd on the bus, the latch
+ * says timeout.  Within the window the transfer is left armed and the
+ * clobbered result outlasted; the window closes on any EP0 completion.  A
+ * genuinely dead device expires it and takes the original failure path.
